From: local <local@gurux-dlms-ts>
Subject: Match replies on the invoke ID alone, ignoring priority and service class

dlms_verifyInvokeId compared the whole invoke-id-and-priority byte of a
reply with the one the client sent. The Hexing HXP100DII answers a 0xC1
request with 0x41, clearing the priority bit, so every reply it sent was
rejected as answering an earlier request.

Compare the low four bits only, which hold the invoke ID.

--- a/development/src/dlms.c
+++ b/development/src/dlms.c
@@ -3913,7 +3913,9 @@ int dlms_getWrapperFrame(
 
 int dlms_verifyInvokeId(dlmsSettings* settings, gxReplyData* reply)
 {
-    if (settings->autoIncreaseInvokeID && reply->invokeId != dlms_getInvokeIDPriority(settings, 0))
+    // Compare only the invoke ID; some meters (e.g. Hexing HXP100DII) clear
+    // the priority bit in their replies.
+    if (settings->autoIncreaseInvokeID && (reply->invokeId & 0x0F) != (settings->invokeID & 0x0F))
     {
         //Invalid invoke ID.
         return DLMS_ERROR_CODE_INVALID_INVOKE_ID;
